*.md
attached_assets/
LICENSE

# Data (will be mounted as volume)
data/
instance/
.last_seen_uid

# --- kept out of git, and therefore out of the image ------------------------
# `COPY . .` reads this file and not .gitignore, so anything deliberately kept
# out of the repository still rides into the image unless it is named here
# too. The two lists had drifted far enough apart that the laptop image was
# 2.68 GB, of which 1.6 GB was .claude/worktrees - six parallel agent sessions'
# full repository checkouts, each holding unmerged work - against 596 KB of
# templates and 264 KB of static files. Production was spared only because the
# Mac mini happens to have no worktrees, not because the mechanism differs.

# Agent session state: worktrees are whole checkouts, and .mcp.json can carry
# server credentials.
.claude/
.worktrees/
.kimi-code/
.mcp.json

# Source bundles (issue #29). These were served unauthenticated from static/,
# which Flask serves directly regardless of any route decorator. .gitignore
# stops them being committed; without these lines an untracked bundle sitting
# in the working tree is still copied in and still served.
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
static/all_code.txt

# Local databases, logs and coverage output. Never build inputs, and a log can
# carry data that has no business in a shipped image.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.log
logs/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ruff_cache/

# Scratch API responses agent sessions leave in the root (#292 follow-up).
nr.json
